    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** headlines our lineup as the premier start with a dominant 78.75 rating. His matchup against Mikolas is exceptionally favorable; beyond the strong park factors and the SP\u2019s bloated 4.77 xERA, **Bryce Harper** carries a significant BvP edge (28 PA) and a robust 0.389 xwOBA, positioning him as our primary engine for production. He is well-supported by **Dylan Beavers**, whose 68.38 rating is fueled by a leadoff role and a 19% SP skill boost, and **Luis Arraez**, who continues to provide elite stability in the four-hole. We are leaning heavily into the favorable matchups against Johnson and Mikolas, where **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Justin Crawford** also project as strong starts due to high park factors and the exploitable nature of the opposing rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today was **Gleyber Torres**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 37.78 efficiency score. Despite his favorable batting order slot, the combination of facing a high-skill arm in Miller (3.39 xERA) and negative park adjustments pushed him below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor.\" We are also monitoring the lower end of the lineup, specifically **Braden Montgomery**, who barely cleared the start threshold at 40.02. His matchup against the southpaw Suarez is a risk, but his switch-hitting utility and park factors kept him active. We are currently navigating a depleted bench with **Cal Raleigh** and **Daulton Varsho** unavailable due to rest or scheduling, forcing us to rely on our core starters to maintain our pursuit of the SB category without compromising our game cap efficiency.",
